112
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:45,721
Don:

113
00:03:45,721 --> 00:03:50,769
Well, we could certainly use some of those examples in our presentation to explain

114
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:54,736
why 90 percent of shoes that people take to recycling centres

115
00:03:54,736 --> 00:03:56,900
or bins get thrown into landfill.

116
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:57,257
Bella:

117
00:03:57,257 --> 00:03:57,614
Mmm.

118
00:03:57,614 --> 00:04:02,609
What did you think about the project his team set up to avoid this

119
00:04:02,609 --> 00:04:06,890
by making new shoes out of the good parts of old shoes?

120
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:07,282
Don:

121
00:04:07,282 --> 00:04:09,635
It sounded like a good idea.

122
00:04:09,635 --> 00:04:14,340
They get so many shoes, they should be able to match parts.

123
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:14,707
Don:

124
00:04:14,707 --> 00:04:17,642
I wasn’t surprised that it failed, though.

125
00:04:17,642 --> 00:04:20,945
I mean who wants to buy second-hand shoes really?

126
00:04:20,945 --> 00:04:23,880
Think of all the germs you could catch!

127
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:24,216
Bella:

128
00:04:24,216 --> 00:04:27,911
Well, people didn’t refuse them for that reason, did they?

129
00:04:27,911 --> 00:04:31,270
It was because the pairs of shoes weren’t identical.

130
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:31,606
Don:

131
00:04:31,606 --> 00:04:34,290
They still managed to ship them overseas, though.

132
00:04:34,290 --> 00:04:34,603
Bella:

133
00:04:34,603 --> 00:04:37,110
That’s another area we need to discuss.

134
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:37,476
Don:

135
00:04:37,476 --> 00:04:42,599
You know I used to consider this topic just from my own perspective, by

136
00:04:42,599 --> 00:04:46,990
thinking about my own recycling behaviour without looking at the bigger picture.

137
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:47,430
Don:

138
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:51,390
So much happens once shoes leave the recycling area.

139
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:51,682
Bella:

140
00:04:51,682 --> 00:04:54,307
It’s not as simple as you first think,

141
00:04:54,307 --> 00:04:58,100
and we can show that by taking a very different approach to it.

142
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,667
Don:

143
00:04:59,667 --> 00:05:01,233
Absolutely.

144
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:07,500
So let’s discuss .

145
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:07,550
.

